    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_AS_READ",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 0.49,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.08,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings level off at about 0.48 from 5 h onward. I diluted the 18 h aliquot to check whether the plate reader was saturating. Diluted 10-fold, the two reads were 0.049 and 0.047, which give 0.48 when multiplied back up. Diluted 4-fold, the two reads were 0.133 and 0.117, which give about 0.50. Both match the undiluted reading of 0.49, so the reader is responding in proportion at this level and the plateau is real (stationary phase), not a reader ceiling. I only tested the 18 h aliquot. I'm assuming the earlier plateau hours behave the same way, since their undiluted readings are almost identical."
  },
